<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Sailana State</h1><p class="st-meta">1736 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Sailana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Rathore Rajput state of western Malwa, an offshoot of Ratlam, later known for its rulers' cactus garden and celebrated cookery.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sailana was founded in 1736 by Jai Singh, a younger member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> ruling house of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ratlam-state">Ratlam</a>, who received his own share of territory in the hills west of Ratlam. The family descended from the Rathores of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scindias">Scindias</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gwalior-state">Gwalior State</a> and later came under British protection within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa-agency">Malwa Agency</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with an 11-gun salute. A Raja governed a small, partly tribal hill territory. In the 20th century the rulers became known for a large cactus garden and for the family's recipes, later published as a well-known cookbook.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, Sailana merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madhya-bharat">Madhya Bharat</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956; it now lies in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ratlam-state">Ratlam</a> district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sailana-state.jpg" alt="Sailana State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Princely_State_of_Sailana.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1736 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sailana</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jai Singh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malvi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sailana</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1842&amp;focus=sailana-state" aria-label="Sailana State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6678 1312 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sailana State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6998 1568L7003 1574M6998 1568L7364 1601M6998 1568L7364 1602M6998 1568L7064 1471"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7003 1574h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7064 1471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6998 1568h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6998 1568h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1842&amp;focus=sailana-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
